  "notes": "Measured on the A321neo. The sharklets' color isn't clear in the photos and is left out. Each aircraft's name in small script under the cockpit and the small Dutch flag by the registration aren't drawn. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on PH-AXB (left side, side-on, Helsinki 2026-09-29): the titles' lengths measured (KLM x 0.165-0.22, Royal Dutch Airlines 0.2245-0.338, fin KLM 0.69 of the chord from 0.25); lowercase 0.7 of the capitals; both titles' baseline is on the window tops (they had run across the windows) and 'KLM' is about 0.42 tall, the crown above it. KLM's 737s carry the same layout; it wasn't re-measured on them (no recent side-on 737-800 photo on Commons).",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximation. KLM's blue-and-white scheme dates from the 1970s; the 2014 refresh is the version with the larger white 'KLM' and 'Royal Dutch Airlines' on the forward fuselage. Older wide-bodies still wearing the pre-2014 titles should be described separately."
